NAME
    dmesg - print the kernel's message log

SYNOPSIS
    dmesg

DESCRIPTION
    Print the kernel's message ring: what it said at boot and since.

SECURITY
    Two checks, for two different questions. The kernel asks whether the
    shell's task holds CAP_KERNEL_LOG. The shell asks whether the person
    logged in is the administrator, because the shell is one task serving
    every login and its capability alone cannot say who is at the
    keyboard. Without the second, every login would read the kernel log.

SEE ALSO
